-- Referential transparency: the same rule, spelled four ways.
--
-- `x WHERE x MEANS e` must be analysed as `e`. Before
-- specs/todo/WHERE-INLINING-SPEC.md only `flat` was found unsatisfiable; the
-- other three hid a limb behind a local name and the contradiction vanished,
-- although every one of them is a top-level decision that IS analysed.
--
-- `parameterised` is the control. A binding that takes arguments stays opaque —
-- substituting under arguments is beta reduction, which this pass does not do —
-- so it must produce NO finding, and it must not lose its arguments on the way.

GIVEN m IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `flat` IF
        m
    AND NOT m

GIVEN m IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `behind a where` IF
        m
    AND NOT e
    WHERE
        e MEANS m

GIVEN m IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `behind a let` IF
    LET e MEANS m
    IN  m AND NOT e

GIVEN m IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `behind two hops` IF
        p
    AND NOT q
    WHERE
        p MEANS q
        q MEANS m

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `parameterised` IF
        `both of` a b
    AND NOT `both of` b a
    WHERE
        GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN, y IS A BOOLEAN
        `both of` x y MEANS x AND y
